Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.27,0:00:09.87,Cap,,0,0,0,,On 5 June 1989, a man in a white shirt\Nwalked into a wide avenue in Beijing,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.27,0:00:11.98,Cap,,0,0,0,,and stopped a column of tanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.89,0:00:17.46,Cap,,0,0,0,,Nobody has ever proved who he\Nwas, or what happened to him.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.15,0:00:22.07,Cap,,0,0,0,,This is the story of the spring\Nthat led to that moment,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.46,0:00:24.86,Cap,,0,0,0,,and of what the world\Ncould see, and could not.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.63,0:00:31.04,Cap,,0,0,0,,It began with a funeral.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.46,0:00:34.69,Cap,,0,0,0,,Hu Yaobang, a Communist\NParty leader seen as a reformer,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.08,0:00:37.44,Cap,,0,0,0,,died on 15 April 1989.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.09,0:00:42.12,Cap,,0,0,0,,Students gathered in Tiananmen\NSquare to mourn him.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.76,0:00:49.02,Cap,,0,0,0,,This is where, forty years ago, Mao\NZedong stepped into the place\Npreviously reserved for emperors,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.46,0:00:53.62,Cap,,0,0,0,,handing down their edicts, and\Nproclaimed the triumph of his\Ncommunist revolution.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.08,0:00:57.62,Cap,,0,0,0,,Tiananmen Square is the heart of\NChina.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.25,0:01:00.49,Cap,,0,0,0,,The mourning was allowed.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.92,0:01:02.98,Cap,,0,0,0,,The demands that followed were not.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.69,0:01:08.77,Cap,,0,0,0,,Their grief soon turned into a protest\Nagainst corruption and rising prices,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.04,0:01:10.74,Cap,,0,0,0,,and a call for political reform.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.46,0:01:14.66,Cap,,0,0,0,,But then their lecturer shot them a\Nzinger,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.86,0:01:20.76,Cap,,0,0,0,,reminding them of the charge that high\Ngovernment and party officials\Nenriched their own families at the\Nexpense of the people.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.46,0:01:25.06,Cap,,0,0,0,,If you want to solve corruption, he\Nsaid, begin with your own sons.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.83,0:01:29.63,Cap,,0,0,0,,On 26 April, the party newspaper,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.80,0:01:33.14,Cap,,0,0,0,,People's Daily, published an\Neditorial about the protest.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.01,0:01:37.07,Cap,,0,0,0,,The editorial said the protest was,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.20,0:01:40.58,Cap,,0,0,0,,in its words, a planned\Nconspiracy and a disturbance.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.55,0:01:45.11,Cap,,0,0,0,,Many students took that\Nas an insult to their grief,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.38,0:01:46.58,Cap,,0,0,0,,and the crowds got bigger.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.47,0:01:51.22,Cap,,0,0,0,,The leadership was\Ndivided on how to respond.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.95,0:01:56.25,Cap,,0,0,0,,Zhao Ziyang, the general\Nsecretary, wanted talks.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.52,0:01:58.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,Hardliners wanted the protest ended.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.55,0:02:03.44,Cap,,0,0,0,,In May, some students\Nbegan a hunger strike.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.23,0:02:08.12,Cap,,0,0,0,,The Soviet leader, Mikhail Gorbachev,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.14,0:02:12.40,Cap,,0,0,0,,was about to arrive for the first Soviet\Nand Chinese summit in thirty years.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.37,0:02:16.57,Cap,,0,0,0,,Foreign reporters had\Ncome to cover the summit.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.88,0:02:18.44,Cap,,0,0,0,,They stayed to cover the Square.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.29,0:02:24.09,Cap,,0,0,0,,The crowds grew beyond students,\Nto workers, teachers and families.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.50,0:02:26.74,Cap,,0,0,0,,Some reports put them at\Nmore than a million people.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.38,0:02:32.38,Cap,,0,0,0,,They defied a government order to be\Nout of the square by the time\NGorbachev arrived,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.34,0:02:34.78,Cap,,0,0,0,,and no one seemed afraid.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.38,0:02:37.28,Cap,,0,0,0,,Student: Why should I be afraid?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.28,0:02:40.88,Cap,,0,0,0,,I'm just a common student.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.65,0:02:46.20,Cap,,0,0,0,,On 19 May, the party\Nleader, Zhao Ziyang,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.22,0:02:48.26,Cap,,0,0,0,,went to the Square to\Nsee the hunger strikers.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.07,0:02:56.66,Cap,,0,0,0,,On 20 May, the government\Ndeclared martial law in Beijing.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.79,0:03:01.18,Cap,,0,0,0,,Troops began to move\Ntoward the centre of the city.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.71,0:03:04.10,Cap,,0,0,0,,The protest did not end.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.79,0:03:09.19,Cap,,0,0,0,,In the last days of May, students\Nraised a statue in the Square.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.82,0:03:11.84,Cap,,0,0,0,,They called it the\NGoddess of Democracy.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.91,0:03:16.99,Cap,,0,0,0,,It stood in front of the portrait\Nof Mao, facing the gate.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.50,0:03:19.16,Cap,,0,0,0,,The government called it an insult.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.97,0:03:24.68,Cap,,0,0,0,,On the night of 3 June, the army\Nmoved on the centre of the city.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.27,0:03:28.10,Cap,,0,0,0,,In the early hours of 4 June,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.12,0:03:31.78,Cap,,0,0,0,,soldiers entered the Square area\Nwith tanks and armoured vehicles.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.06,0:03:39.20,Cap,,0,0,0,,Tiananmen Square of course is firmly\Nin the hands of the military,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.70,0:03:46.70,Cap,,0,0,0,,and what once was this country's\Nsymbol of power is now its symbol of\Ntragedy and shame.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.61,0:03:51.32,Cap,,0,0,0,,Soldiers fired on people in the\Nstreets around the Square.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.25,0:03:55.96,Cap,,0,0,0,,No one has ever established\Nhow many people died.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.92,0:04:05.22,Cap,,0,0,0,,We don't know to this moment how many\Npeople were killed and wounded in the\Narmy's attack on the people of\NBeijing,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.02,0:04:07.92,Cap,,0,0,0,,the number is certainly in the\Nhundreds.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.77,0:04:12.50,Cap,,0,0,0,,A State Department situation\Nreport listed estimates
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.52,0:04:14.72,Cap,,0,0,0,,from five hundred to\Ntwenty six hundred.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.61,0:04:17.73,Cap,,0,0,0,,The Chinese government said
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.75,0:04:19.89,Cap,,0,0,0,,that more than two\Nhundred people were killed,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.60,0:04:22.08,Cap,,0,0,0,,thirty six of them students.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.13,0:04:27.85,Cap,,0,0,0,,A United States State Department\Nsummary at the time gave a range
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.26,0:04:30.48,Cap,,0,0,0,,of one hundred eighty to five hundred.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.35,0:04:34.47,Cap,,0,0,0,,Other estimates run\Ninto the thousands.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.94,0:04:36.94,Cap,,0,0,0,,None of these figures\Nhas been confirmed.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.85,0:04:42.37,Cap,,0,0,0,,Foreign broadcasters had lost their\Nsatellite links under martial law.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.96,0:04:44.84,Cap,,0,0,0,,Reporters phoned in what they could.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.54,0:04:51.24,Cap,,0,0,0,,Forest, night has fallen here. It's\Nawfully quiet at the moment.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.54,0:04:56.24,Cap,,0,0,0,,In the afternoon we were able to hear\Nsome firing out in the west.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.94,0:04:58.54,Cap,,0,0,0,,The source of it is very uncertain.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.04,0:05:02.44,Cap,,0,0,0,,We cannot say for sure whether it was\Nbetween rival army units.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.07,0:05:11.05,Cap,,0,0,0,,On 5 June, a column of tanks rolled\Neast along Chang'an Avenue,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.42,0:05:13.24,Cap,,0,0,0,,the wide road beside the Square.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.19,0:05:18.53,Cap,,0,0,0,,A man in a white shirt and\Ndark trousers, carrying bags,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.82,0:05:20.90,Cap,,0,0,0,,stepped into the road\Nin front of the first tank.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.97,0:05:24.12,Cap,,0,0,0,,The tanks stopped.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.79,0:05:28.43,Cap,,0,0,0,,The Associated Press\Ncounted eighteen tanks,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.86,0:05:31.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,and said the standoff held them\Nup for about three minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.41,0:05:35.73,Cap,,0,0,0,,When the lead tank tried\Nto steer around him,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.02,0:05:37.72,Cap,,0,0,0,,he moved into its path again.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.37,0:05:42.08,Cap,,0,0,0,,Then he climbed onto the\Ntank and spoke to the crew.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.87,0:05:45.97,Cap,,0,0,0,,How long it lasted\Ndepends on the account,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.08,0:05:48.54,Cap,,0,0,0,,from about three\Nminutes to six or seven.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.41,0:05:52.93,Cap,,0,0,0,,Then people came out of the\Ncrowd and led him away.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.38,0:05:55.32,Cap,,0,0,0,,Witnesses disagree\Nabout who they were.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.97,0:05:59.04,Cap,,0,0,0,,The scene was\Nphotographed and filmed
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.06,0:06:01.16,Cap,,0,0,0,,from hotel balconies and rooftops.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.95,0:06:05.26,Cap,,0,0,0,,Television networks\Ncarried it around the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.19,0:06:09.37,Cap,,0,0,0,,That Monday, President George H.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.58,0:06:09.68,Cap,,0,0,0,,W.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.70,0:06:12.50,Cap,,0,0,0,,Bush suspended American\Narms sales to China.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.35,0:06:17.24,Cap,,0,0,0,,Bush said that the image\Nwould be with us a long time.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.86,0:06:23.96,Cap,,0,0,0,,All of us have seen the bravery and\Nthe determination of the students and\Nthe workers,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.86,0:06:28.06,Cap,,0,0,0,,and all I can say to him, wherever he\Nmight be,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.32,0:06:29.56,Cap,,0,0,0,,or to the people around the world,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.86,0:06:33.96,Cap,,0,0,0,,is we are and we must stand with him.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.61,0:06:39.76,Cap,,0,0,0,,About two weeks later,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.85,0:06:43.69,Cap,,0,0,0,,the Sunday Express in London\Nnamed him as Wang Weilin,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.71,0:06:44.94,Cap,,0,0,0,,a nineteen year old student.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.67,0:06:48.58,Cap,,0,0,0,,That name has never been confirmed.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.27,0:06:52.56,Cap,,0,0,0,,Inside China, the image is censored.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.25,0:06:56.97,Cap,,0,0,0,,Party documents, reported\Nby a Hong Kong rights group,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.40,0:07:00.86,Cap,,0,0,0,,said officials could not find him\Namong the dead or the prisoners.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.91,0:07:06.52,Cap,,0,0,0,,In 1990, Jiang Zemin,\Nthen the party leader,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.54,0:07:09.23,Cap,,0,0,0,,was asked on American\Ntelevision what became of him.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.82,0:07:11.98,Cap,,0,0,0,,He said he thought the\Nman was never killed.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.83,0:07:16.47,Cap,,0,0,0,,Ten years later he said the\Nman was never arrested,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.54,0:07:18.28,Cap,,0,0,0,,and that he did not\Nknow where he was.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.05,0:07:21.91,Cap,,0,0,0,,Other accounts say he was executed.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.28,0:07:23.67,Cap,,0,0,0,,Others say he is alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.22,0:07:25.68,Cap,,0,0,0,,No account has been proved.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.57,0:07:28.92,Cap,,0,0,0,,On 21 June,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.07,0:07:30.78,Cap,,0,0,0,,a State Department\Nsummary reported
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.80,0:07:32.87,Cap,,0,0,0,,more than fifteen\Nhundred people arrested,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.15,0:07:34.50,Cap,,0,0,0,,among them student leaders.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.33,0:07:39.79,Cap,,0,0,0,,Washington suspended military\Nsales and high level contacts,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.36,0:07:42.58,Cap,,0,0,0,,and Congress pressed\Nfor wider sanctions.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.71,0:07:46.56,Cap,,0,0,0,,The United States has since called
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.58,0:07:49.18,Cap,,0,0,0,,on the Chinese government\Nto account for those killed,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.29,0:07:50.50,Cap,,0,0,0,,detained or missing.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.23,0:07:55.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,A man stood in front of the tanks, and\Nthen he vanished from the record.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.25,0:07:59.38,Cap,,0,0,0,,Who was he, and what\Nhappened to him?
